{{!--
    reference/schema-tools - the filter box and expand/collapse pair that sit beside a
    large schema's heading.

    Params:
      scope - id of the element holding the property rows these act on (required)
      label - what is being filtered, used as the placeholder and the accessible name,
              e.g. "Filter response fields" (required)

    Rendered only for schemas past a size threshold (see reference/operation): on a
    three-property body a filter is noise, and a tag page would otherwise carry two dozen
    of them. Behavior lives in static/js/reference.js, keyed off data-schema-tools and the
    data-schema-scope id - the page itself is server-rendered and works without it, which
    is why the controls degrade to a plain input and two buttons that simply do nothing if
    the script never loads.

    The script finds the input and the buttons by their position inside this container
    rather than by hook attributes, so the shared ui/* partials can be used unchanged.
--}}
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-schema-tools data-schema-scope="{{scope}}">
    {{> ui/search-input placeholder=label class="w-48" id="" name="" value="" type="" shortcut="" shortcutMac=""}}
    {{> ui/btn label="Expand all" bare=true style="text" size="xs" icon="" id="" class="" type=""}}
    {{> ui/btn label="Collapse all" bare=true style="text" size="xs" icon="" id="" class="" type=""}}
    <span class="text-base-content/50 text-xs" data-schema-count role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
</div>
